<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49650" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulna</span></b> , ae, f.
		Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠλένη</span>; Goth. aleina; Germ.
			Elle; cf. Ellenbogen; Engl. ell, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the elbow.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				43, 98, § 243</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, in gen., <i>the
			arm</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tremula patris dormientis in ulnā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					17, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 18</span></i> (3, 10), 9; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				847</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 652</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 63</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			664</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 3, 457</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 499</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat.
				S. 5, 3, 266 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> As a measure of length. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>An ell</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 3,
				105</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. G. 3, 355</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod. 4,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 748</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> As much as
			a man can clasp with both arms, <i>a fathom</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				40, 76, § 202</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
